## 6. Color system

**Source of truth:** `tailwind.config.ts`. NEVER use arbitrary hex (`bg-[#143D30]`) or default Tailwind palette (`blue-500`, `indigo-600`, `gray-200`) for product chrome.

| Token | Tailwind class | Use for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| primary | `bg-primary`, `text-primary` | Brand forest — headers, primary buttons, trust surfaces |
| primary-fg | `text-primary-fg` | Text/icons on `bg-primary` |
| secondary | `bg-secondary`, `text-secondary` | Lime accent — hero CTAs, emphasis words, chip hover borders |
| accent | `ring-accent`, `focus:border-accent`, `outline-accent` | Focus rings, mint highlights |
| body | `text-body` | Primary text on light surfaces |
| muted | `text-muted` | Secondary text, labels, meta |
| surface | `bg-surface` | Cards, panels |
| surface-elevated | `bg-surface-elevated` | Hover/elevated chips |
| bg-light | `bg-bg-light` | Page sections, inputs, chip backgrounds |
| bg-dark | `bg-bg-dark` | Dark mode page base |
| border | `border-border` | All structural borders |
| error | `text-error`, border/text for errors | Validation, destructive hints |
| warning | `bg-warning` (solid), `bg-warning/10`, `border-warning/40` | Warning/pending surfaces, progress-at-limit |
| warning-fg | `text-warning-fg` | Readable text/icons on warning surfaces (amber `text-warning` alone fails contrast — never use it for body text) |
| gold | `bg-gold`, `text-gold-fg`, `border-gold-edge` | **Reserved** max-visibility action (Save/Follow search) — see gold subsection below |

### Color rules

- **Primary CTA (in-app):** `rounded-full bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-primary-fg` with `hover:brightness-110` or `hover:brightness-95`.
- **Hero / high-energy CTA on green:** `bg-secondary text-primary` (lime button on forest hero).
- **Secondary CTA:** `rounded-full border border-border bg-surface` with `hover:bg-surface-elevated`.
- **Accent sparingly:** `secondary` signals energy — not full-page lime backgrounds.
- **Success/info banners:** `border-secondary/40 bg-secondary/10` (see `SavedSearchesPage`).
- **Warning banners/boxes:** `border border-warning/40 bg-warning/10 text-warning-fg` (see email-verify banner). Icons/emphasis `text-warning-fg`; solid `bg-warning` only for indicators like progress bars.
- **Error banners:** `border border-error/30 bg-error/5 text-error`.
- On `bg-primary` hero: text `text-primary-fg`; emphasized phrase `text-secondary`.

### CTA decision tree (which treatment to use)

Pick exactly one treatment per action, in this priority order:

1. **Is it the single most important conversion action on the screen** (Save/Follow search)? → **gold** (`bg-gold text-gold-fg`). Max one per screen.
2. **Is it the main action of the view** (Publicar, Buscar, Guardar cambios, Enviar)? → **primary** (`rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-fg hover:brightness-110`).
3. **Is it on the forest hero / dark surface**? → **lime** (`bg-secondary text-primary`).
4. **Is it a supporting / secondary action** (Cancelar, Volver, secondary link-buttons)? → **bordered surface** (`rounded-full border border-border bg-surface hover:bg-surface-elevated`).
5. **Is it destructive** (Eliminar, Cerrar sesión)? → **error** intent (`text-error`, `hover:bg-error/5`); confirm in a dialog for irreversible actions.

If two actions on one screen both want primary/gold, demote the lesser one — never show two golds or competing equal-weight primaries side by side.

### Gold — reserved maximum-visibility accent

A single **gold** treatment is reserved for the **highest-priority conversion action only** — currently the **Save / Follow search** control (`src/components/search/SaveSearchButton.tsx`). It is a real token in `tailwind.config.ts` (`gold`), **not** a general-purpose accent.

| Role | Class |
| --- | --- |
| Fill | `bg-gold` (follow half: `bg-gold/90`) |
| Hover / active fill | `hover:bg-gold-hover`, `active:bg-gold-active` |
| Border / dividers | `border-gold-edge` (`/60`–`/70` for inner splits), hover `border-gold-edge-hover` |
| Text / icon | `text-gold-fg` (dark, for contrast — never white on gold) |
| Focus ring | `ring-gold-ring/50` (forest — ties gold back to the brand, not lime) |

**Gold rules:**

- **One gold action per screen, maximum.** It means "the single most important thing to do here" — overuse destroys its salience.
- Reserved for Save/Follow search. Do **not** put gold on primary CTAs, nav, chips, banners, badges, or destructive actions — those stay on `primary` / `secondary` / `error`.
- Always `text-gold-fg` on gold; pair with the forest focus ring (`ring-gold-ring`) and green pulse ring, never a lime ring.
- The green pulse ring stroke in `PulseRing` uses the forest hex as an SVG `stroke` attribute — SVG stroke/fill attributes are the one place raw hex is unavoidable (Tailwind classes do not apply). Keep it aligned with `gold-ring`.

## 7. Typography

- **Font:** `font-sans` → Inter (loaded in app). Do not introduce other font families.
- **Page titles:** `text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight` → `sm:text-4xl` / `md:text-5xl` on marketing hero.
- **Section titles:** `text-lg font-semibold text-body` or `font-bold text-primary` (legal).
- **Labels:** `text-sm font-medium text-body`.
- **Meta / overlines:** `text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted`.
- **Body:** `text-sm leading-relaxed text-body` or `text-base` on hero subcopy.
- **Weights:** `font-semibold` on buttons; `font-bold` on major headings only. Avoid `font-black`.

## 8. Shape, spacing, elevation

### Border radius (match existing components)

| Element | Class |
| --- | --- |
| Primary/secondary buttons | `rounded-full` |
| Cards, modals, panels | `rounded-2xl` |
| Inputs, sheet actions | `rounded-xl` |
| Tags/chips | `rounded-full` |
| Logo fallback mark | `rounded-lg` |
| Small map controls | `rounded-lg` |

Do **not** use `rounded-3xl` on forms/cards unless matching an existing pattern in the same feature.

### Spacing

- Prefer Tailwind scale on **4px grid**: `p-4`, `p-5`, `p-6`, `gap-2`, `gap-3`, `gap-4`.
- Page gutters: `px-4 sm:px-6`; content max widths `max-w-3xl` (legal), `max-w-6xl` / `max-w-7xl` (marketing).
- Touch targets: at least `min-h-11` or `min-h-12` on primary actions (mobile-first).

### Elevation

- **Default:** flat cards with `border border-border bg-surface` — light `shadow-sm` on cards/modals is OK.
- **Hero CTA:** `shadow-lg` / `shadow-md` allowed on lime CTAs only.
- Prefer **borders over heavy shadows** (`shadow-xl` rare — modals like `PropertyRoomDetailModal` only).
- Focus: `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-secondary/40` or global `outline-accent` (`src/index.css`).

## 9. Dark mode

- Mechanism: `class="dark"` on `<html>` (`darkMode: "class"` in Tailwind).
- Global overrides in `src/index.css` remap `.text-body`, `.bg-surface`, `.border-border`, etc.
- Use **semantic tokens** (`bg-surface`, `text-body`, `border-border`) so dark mode inherits — avoid hardcoding `dark:bg-gray-800` on new components unless matching an existing footer pattern.
- `dark:` variant on `text-primary` maps to mint (`accent`) — intentional for links in dark mode.

## 10. Logo and brand assets

**Component:** `src/components/BrandLogo.tsx` — always use this instead of raw `<img src="/brand/...">` for the wordmark.

| Variant | When | Assets |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `onLight` (default) | White/light surfaces (header, footer) | `/brand/logo-lockup.svg` |
| `onDark` | `bg-primary` hero, dark green backgrounds | `/brand/logo-lockup-on-dark.svg` |

**Other assets (`public/brand/`):**

- `logo-mark.svg`, `mark-white.svg` — icon/mark only when lockup does not fit.
- `hero-art.svg` — decorative hero illustration via `HeroBrandArt` (low opacity, never competing with copy).
- `meta-app-icon-1024.png` — Meta / app icon submissions only.

**Logo rules:** Do not recolor, stretch, or rotate lockups. Alt text pattern: `Bestie — inicio`. Footer: `© {year} Bestie™`.

## 11. Imagery

- Listing photos: real rooms/homes; bright, honest, lived-in — not stock corporate office imagery.
- Hero art: optional, soft (`opacity-[0.22]`–`0.28`), `pointer-events-none`, `aria-hidden`.
- Empty/placeholder states: neutral `bg-bg-light` / `border-border`, not generic gray placeholders.

## 12. Motion and interaction

- Transitions: `transition hover:brightness-95`, `hover:brightness-110`, `active:scale-[0.99]` on primary buttons — subtle only.
- No bounce/spring animations on forms or wizards.
- Hero may use soft blurred lime orb (`bg-secondary/20 blur-3xl`) as atmosphere — do not replicate on dense data UI.

### Attention / pulse-ring pattern

To draw one-time attention to a high-value control (the Save-search pulse), reuse the existing pattern in `SaveSearchButton.tsx` (`PulseRing` + the `autosave-ring-travel` keyframes in `src/index.css`) — do **not** invent new attention animations:

- A single forest-green ring travels the control's outline once, then fades (`animation … forwards`, not looping) — attention without nagging.
- Reserve it for the gold Save-search control and equivalent top-priority moments; never run it on multiple elements at once.
- Pair with the gold treatment and the forest ring color; keep the SVG `stroke` aligned with `gold-ring`.
- Nudges/tooltips that accompany it must escape parent overflow and sit at the correct layer (`.cursor/rules/ui-layering-precedence.mdc`) — avoid `overflow-hidden` on their containers.

## 13. Accessibility floor

Non-negotiable minimums (the codebase already meets these — do not regress them):

- **Contrast:** body/label text must stay legible on its surface. On `bg-gold`, always use `text-gold-fg` (dark) — never white. Don't put `text-muted` on `bg-secondary`/colored fills where it drops below readable contrast.
- **Focus visible:** every interactive element keeps a visible focus state — rely on the global `:focus-visible` outline (`src/index.css`) or an explicit `focus-visible:ring-2`. Never `outline-none` without a replacement ring.
- **Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`** in Spanish (e.g. `aria-label="Cerrar"`, `aria-label="Guardar búsqueda"`). Decorative icons/art get `aria-hidden`.
- **Touch targets:** primary actions at least `min-h-11`/`min-h-12`; don't shrink tap areas below ~40px on mobile.
- **Semantics:** status messages use `role="status"`; errors use `role="alert"`; modals set `role="dialog"`/`aria-modal` and a labelled title (see `AccountEditPage` reset dialog).
- **Motion:** attention animations play once and stop; no infinite motion behind text.

## 14. UI layering

Floating UI z-index stacks are defined in `.cursor/rules/ui-layering-precedence.mdc`. Do not invent new z-index tiers; portal modals to `document.body` when specified there.

## 15. Anti-patterns (NEVER)

- Default Tailwind blues/indigos (`bg-blue-600`, `bg-indigo-600`, `border-indigo-200`) for product UI.
- Arbitrary hex or rgb in Tailwind class names — every brand color (including **gold**, see §6) is a token. The only place raw hex is allowed is inside SVG `stroke`/`fill` attributes, where Tailwind classes cannot reach.
- English UI strings, Title Case headings, or multiple exclamation marks.
- Generic SaaS copy (“streamline”, “leverage”, “supercharge”).
- Luxury real-estate tone (“residencia exclusiva”, “inversión inmobiliaria”) for roommate listings.
- New logo SVGs or recolored wordmarks outside `public/brand/`.
- Emoji in core app chrome (search, publish wizard, listing detail, profile).
- Childish voice (“¡Hola bestie! 🎉”) on transactional screens.
- Replacing **roomie/bestie** positioning with cold “inquilino/arrendatario” in marketing.

